From 0817ee83f33298f8c77a7e03d1a19ac624832bef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:42:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 117/120] gpu/vulkan, core: device fixes from the DS2 port
 (Mali defaults, closing crash, stall log, memory cuts)

- vulkan_arm_driver_defaults: on Arm's proprietary Mali driver, render passes instead of dynamic
  rendering and restricted render areas, where nothing else set them.
- Occlusion queries end outside the render pass and only once (Arm driver fault).
- POSIX threads cache their kernel tid at start: pthread_gettid_np aborted on a joined thread when
  TerminateTitle woke every guest thread.
- vulkan_gpu_stall_log_ms: blocking fence waits and frames over 250 ms are logged (release too).
- upload_buffer_max_free_mb and vulkan_evict_idle_render_targets_s (off by default here; the app
  turns them on), GPU memory by kind every vulkan_log_device_memory_s, SyncLoggingToStorage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

